# L §5.11 step 2: a `v` on a `replace rule` "may name only that version and adds nothing".  `v v2` inside v2 is
# the same as no v: from 2026-07 the replaced base gives 1, before it the def's own base gives 0.
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"

def x: int at reader
  rule base = 0

version v2
  cite s
  governs 2026-07..
  known 2026-06-01
  replace rule x.base v v2 = 1

ask q1: x law 2026-03-01
ask q2: x law 2026-08-01
=== expect
q1: 0
  law date 2026-03-01, cut 2026-12-31
q2: 1
  law date 2026-08-01, cut 2026-12-31
